  "markdown": "Where we work\n\n# Wallpaper installation in Mayfair\n\nHotels, townhouses and apartments in Mayfair, W1. Our longest recent commission in the area was Brown's Hotel on Albemarle Street, where Mr Wallcover was the main decorating contractor from 2022 to 2024.\n\n[Start your project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/) [See the work](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/)\n\nMayfair rooms tend to carry expensive materials: hand-painted scenic papers, silk, grasscloth and fabric walling. They are also rooms that stay in use while the work goes on, whether that is a hotel floor with guests or a house with a household.\n\nAt Brown's Hotel the package was wallcoverings, fine painting, French polishing and other specialist finishes, carried out room by room around a working hotel. The same approach applies to a single drawing room: a contained work area, protection of floors and joinery, and a tidy room at the end of each day.\n\nWe survey on site, write the scope room by room, and quantify the paper with the repeat and the wastage it needs. If the paper is supplied by your designer, we receive it, check it against the measure, and hang what was specified.\n\nBrown's is one of three published Mayfair jobs. On Grosvenor Square, at the hotel that is now [The Biltmore Mayfair](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/biltmore-mayfair/) (then the Millennium Hotel), we installed a guest-room wallcovering programme of more than 15,000 m² in 2018, on a schedule that included Phillip Jeffries. On Savile Row, from April 2018 to March 2019, we installed [Huntsman](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/huntsman-savile-row/)'s bespoke printed wallpaper, a print of the Huntsman tweed, and covered the display boards in the same print.\n\n![Narrow bedside at Brown's Hotel, Mayfair, papered in pale tree-and-leaf wallcovering, with a sculptural bronze lamp, a wall light and a green patterned headboard.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/browns-hotel-mayfair-10-800.webp)\n\nOur work in Mayfair: a finished guest room at [Brown's Hotel](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/browns-hotel-mayfair/), Albemarle Street, W1. Photograph: Mr Wallcover.\n\n## On the public record\n\n[![Finished guest bedroom at Brown's Hotel, Mayfair: pale tree-and-leaf wallcovering behind a green patterned headboard, with velvet and fringed botanical cushions under lit wall lights.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/browns-hotel-mayfair-09-800.webp)](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/browns-hotel-mayfair/)\n\nFinished guest bedroom at Brown's Hotel, Mayfair: pale tree-and-leaf wallcovering behind a green patterned headboard, with velvet and fringed botanical cushions under lit wall lights. Photograph: Mr Wallcover.\n\n### [Brown's Hotel, Mayfair](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/browns-hotel-mayfair/)\n\nMain decorating contractor, 2022–2024.\n\n[View the project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/browns-hotel-mayfair/)\n\n[![Hotel bedroom with grasscloth-effect wallcovering, navy armchair and full-height curtains, the Millennium Hotel, Grosvenor Square, now The Biltmore Mayfair.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/biltmore-02-800.webp)](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/biltmore-mayfair/)\n\nHotel bedroom with grasscloth-effect wallcovering, navy armchair and full-height curtains, the Millennium Hotel, Grosvenor Square, now The Biltmore Mayfair. Photograph: Mr Wallcover.\n\n### [The Biltmore Mayfair](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/biltmore-mayfair/)\n\nGuest-room wallcoverings, including a Phillip Jeffries schedule, 2018.\n\n[View the project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/biltmore-mayfair/)\n\n[![Huntsman, Savile Row: a tweed-print wallpapered room with a sofa and dartboard.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/huntsman-07-800.webp)](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/huntsman-savile-row/)\n\nHuntsman, Savile Row: a tweed-print wallpapered room with a sofa and dartboard. Photograph: Mr Wallcover.\n\n### [Huntsman, Savile Row](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/huntsman-savile-row/)\n\nBespoke printed wallpaper installation and display boards, 2018–2019.\n\n[View the project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/huntsman-savile-row/)\n\nQuestions\n\n## Questions about papering in Mayfair\n\nIllustrative material studies\n\nPause motion\n\n### Do you work in occupied houses and hotels in Mayfair?\n\nYes. Most of our Mayfair work has been in rooms that stay in use. At Brown's Hotel the decorating package ran from 2022 to 2024 around a working hotel. Work areas are contained and left tidy each day.\n\n### How do you price wallpaper hanging in Mayfair?\n\nFrom a site survey or from drawings. The figure follows the measured area after openings are taken off, the pattern repeat, the state of the walls and the material. There is no flat rate per roll.\n\n## What happens next\n\n1. Dorin Burcus reads your note.\n2. You can book a 20-minute call to talk the project through.\n3. If the project needs a survey, we arrange it after we have spoken.\n4. After the survey we write a scope of works by room.\n\n[Start your project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/)\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder · Last reviewed 9 October 2026\n",
